1
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:06,500
Rise and shine.

2
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:08,220
Welcome to Morio Radio.

3
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:11,020
As usual, this is your host, Kai Harada,

4
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,537
keeping you company on this fine morning,

5
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,561
and I've got just the song
to start you off right.

6
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:36,760
Now, let's dig in, shall we?

7
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:40,811
Oh, but before we begin, I have
a little something for you.

8
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:10,960
Thank you.

9
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:35,117
If it doesn't live in peace, I'm
not going to be getting for hair,

10
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,860
but I'm not going to be in breath.

11
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:41,800
I'm not going to be calling
you one of the times,

12
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:45,620
but you might see
yourself being beautiful.

13
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,957
What are you talking about?

14
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:48,870
Chasing.

15
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:56,177
I'm going to be chasing.

16
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:57,360
I'll chase you!

17
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:59,780
I'll chase you tomorrow!

18
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:02,660
I'll do it again, and I'll do it again!

19
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:06,575
I'll give you the future,
and I'll give you the future!

20
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:10,700
I'll give you the future,
so I'll chase you!

21
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:19,060
Excuse me, Mr. Kira?

22
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:25,320
Mr. Kira,

23
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,257
I know this is super last minute,

24
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:30,458
but would you be interested
in getting lunch with us?

25
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,840
Apologies, but I must decline.

26
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:37,477
I need to finish delivering these
documents before the day gets away from me.

27
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:38,560
Enjoy your lunch.

28
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:42,646
Don't waste your time on him.

29
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,678
He'd suck the life out of the party.

30
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:48,137
The guys and I invite him out on occasion,

31
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:51,338
but we can never tell if
he's having fun or hates us.

32
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:54,400
Yoshikage Kira, age 33, single.

33
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:59,237
He's a model employee, that's for damn
sure, but the guy's dull as dishwater.

34
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:01,997
It's not that he's necessarily
a tool or anything.

35
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:04,240
He's just kind of blah, you know?

36
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:12,080
Oh, is that right?

37
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:14,757
Someone's a little bent out of shape.

38
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:16,857
Some new girls at work
invited me to lunch.

39
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:18,877
Really, it's as innocent as that.

40
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:21,725
But I promised you lunch
was our time together.

41
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:25,632
I'd never go back in my word
just to fraternize with them.

42
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:28,413
You heard me turn them down, didn't you?

43
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:33,257
In the time we've known each other,
I've never left you by your lonesome.

44
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:34,170
Right?

45
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:36,840
Good, it's settled.

46
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:40,577
Now stop this silly fretting and
let's pick out some sandwiches.

47
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:42,097
Now, which one do you want?

48
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:44,880
Mmm, this one has a delicate texture.

49
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,137
This bakery's one of my favorites.

50
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:50,197
It makes sandwiches with
bread made fresh at 11 a .m.

51
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,797
They're all the rage around here.

52
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:54,998
You'd be lucky to find one
on the shelf after 1 p .m.

53
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:58,417
Even through the wrapper, you can
feel they're fresh from the oven.

54
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:02,265
The katsu they use is always
freshly fried and perfectly crispy.

55
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,360
What have we here?

56
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:10,326
It seems in all the excitement, you managed
to tear the wrapper and make a mess.

57
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:12,040
Such a naughty girl.

58
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:30,700
It's a waste, but this
sandwich is ruined now.

59
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:33,568
I suppose we'll just
buy the one underneath.

60
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:35,689
Thank you for dropping by.

61
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:55,717
simply beautiful isn't it quaint
little Mario between us it might be

62
00:04:55,800 --> 00:05:00,260
the most marvelous town on earth
it's like we're on a romantic picnic

63
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:16,220
A bit aromatic for my taste.

64
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:19,382
I think it's time for the
two of us to part ways.

65
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:21,231
The end is close at hand.

66
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:22,920
Close at hand.

67
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:25,700
If luck is on my side,

68
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:30,409
perhaps I'll cross paths with a beautiful
new girl visiting from out of town.

69
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:38,700
Oh joy, it's a mutt.

70
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:43,730
Uh-oh!

71
00:05:58,860 --> 00:05:59,690
Huh?

72
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:00,970
Shigechi!

73
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:02,660
Ah? Hey!

74
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:07,400
Josuke and Okuyasu, good
to see you! What's up?

75
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:10,237
You know, you got here
just in the nick of time.

76
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:12,097
I'll get right to the point, okay?

77
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:13,777
We need to borrow some lunch money.

78
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:16,157
We're a little strapped
for cash at the moment.

79
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:17,070
Huh?

80
00:06:17,153 --> 00:06:18,371
How's that even possible?

81
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:20,857
What happened to the money we
got from the lottery ticket?

82
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:22,058
Is it gone already?

83
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:23,460
Don't be silly.

84
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:24,997
We put all that in the bank.

85
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,057
And you gotta be crazy
if you think we go all

86
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:29,177
the way to the bank just
to get some lunch money.

87
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:30,597
It's not worth the walk.

88
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,857
A thousand yen should be
enough for both of us.

89
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:33,770
I agree.

90
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:37,797
Come on, as soon as school's over,
we'll head to the bank and pay you back.

91
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,237
Hey, I know that logo.

92
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:41,080
You got a sandwich from St.

93
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:42,177
Gentleman, didn't you?

94
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:43,597
Whoa, what do you know?

95
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,637
I thought they were sold out.

96
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:48,277
They are, and you're not getting a
single bite of mine, you got that?

97
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:51,717
If you leave my sandwich alone,
I'll lend you guys the money.

98
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:54,094
Sweet, I can taste their lunch already.

99
00:06:55,460 --> 00:06:56,290
Thank you.

100
00:06:56,760 --> 00:07:00,197
And just so you know, I'm writing
an I-O-U for this little loan.

101
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:02,317
You're not gonna weasel out of this one.

102
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:04,757
Me, you're the biggest weasel there is.

103
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:07,237
Okay, June 24th.

104
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:12,280
Lent 1,000 yen to needy
friends. Hang on. Lent.

105
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,577
How do you write the
character for Lent again?

106
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:15,490
Oh, well.

107
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:17,015
This'll work for now.

108
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:20,154
I guess Hiragana's better than nothing.

109
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:21,430
Crud, monkeys.

110
00:07:21,513 --> 00:07:24,197
I don't know how to write
Josuke or Okuyasu, either.

111
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:25,600
Huh? What the?

112
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:27,537
My sandwich was right there.

113
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:28,561
Where did it go?

114
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:35,480
What a relief!

115
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,600
My sandwich is safe and sound!

116
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:41,720
I don't remember being this far
away, but at least I found it!

117
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:53,117
Th-that's...

118
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:56,000
Hey Josuke! Okuyasu! Wait up!

119
00:07:56,180 --> 00:07:57,277
We're not done yet!

120
00:07:57,360 --> 00:08:00,640
I need your thumbprints on
my IOU to make it official!

121
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:07,120
You have got to be kidding me.

122
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:10,180
That lump of a brat
grabbed my back by mistake.

123
00:08:11,020 --> 00:08:13,297
Come on, could you be any more annoying?

124
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:15,317
How would we give you our thumbprints?

125
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,230
It's simple.

126
00:08:16,313 --> 00:08:18,377
You cut your thumb with a
knife and use the blood.

127
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:19,617
What are you talking about?

128
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:21,117
We don't have to go that far.

129
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:23,612
Just sign the IOU and we'll call it good.

130
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:28,400
Yeah, yeah, but let's haul ass to sink
gentlemen before they sell out. Damn it.

131
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:30,954
I can't let him see what's in that bag.

132
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:34,917
She's still wearing the ring I
put on her finger this morning.

133
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,840
It has my fingerprints on it.

134
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:39,257
So when the police open an investigation,

135
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:43,046
it'll be just a matter of time
before they trace it back to me.

136
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:49,187
Yoshikage Kira has been
at this for 15 years,

137
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:52,399
and in all that time, he's
never left a single clue.

138
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:54,917
This pathetic whelp isn't changing that.

139
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,500
Hey, Josuke, let's head in. Right.

140
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:01,033
I'll stay outside and wait for you guys.

141
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:05,000
My best bet is to take it by force.

142
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:09,649
On second thought, I'd better
snatch it without his knowing.

143
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:15,390
Shigechi!

144
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,957
You're a lucky son of
a gun, you know that?

145
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:20,977
The lunchtime rush beat us here,
and they're already out of St.

146
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,157
Gentleman's Sandwiches.

147
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,070
Just our luck.

148
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,030
They're sold out, huh?

149
00:09:24,113 --> 00:09:25,780
Well, isn't that a shame?

150
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:28,400
I feel bad for you guys, I really do.

151
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:33,151
I guess I could sell you mine, but so
you know it'll cost you 10,000 yen, k?

152
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:38,460
Boy, not a decent bone
in your body, is there?

153
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:41,737
All right, Josuke, looks
like we're headed to Hokuben.

154
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:43,408
You sure that'll be enough?

155
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:46,560
I doubt a 500 yen meal and
a drink will fill us up.

156
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:47,917
We're better off skipping it.

157
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,437
It's not my first choice, but
the cafeteria will do just fine.

158
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,777
Besides, that's where Koichi
said he's getting lunch today.

159
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:57,260
Aw, man, that means he'll be
there with Yukako Yamagishi.

160
00:09:57,600 --> 00:10:01,659
I hate having to be the third wheel
to those Honeymooners' love fest.

161
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,118
And the food they serve is terrible.

162
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:07,117
Their nasty meat is so thin,
it's practically invisible.

163
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:10,277
And who knows what kind of weird
shit they put in the miso soup.

164
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:13,317
Hey, why don't we use the equipment
room at my middle school's gym?

165
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:15,357
It has tons of drinks to choose from.

166
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,717
Our PE teacher always
sneaks away to have his

167
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,837
coffee and tea in there
when no one's looking.

168
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:22,157
All the teachers are in the
faculty room during lunch,

169
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:24,037
so they won't be able to bust us.

170
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:27,917
Sometimes I'll sneak in through the
window and take a cup to quench my thirst.

171
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,757
Why don't you go buy lunch and we'll
hang out there and eat together?

172
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,317
Let's back it up there, Shigechi.

173
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:34,617
Are you seriously stealing
drinks from school?

174
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:36,100
You stingy bastard.

175
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:38,297
Can't you even buy drinks for yourself?

176
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:40,857
You never see me doing
something that greedy.

177
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:41,880
See you later.

178
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,677
Geez, what crawled up there butts?

179
00:10:44,760 --> 00:10:46,466
I was just trying to be nice.

180
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:50,480
Okay, well, you better pay me
back my 1,000 yen tomorrow.

181
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:04,602
Sorry for bumping into you, sir.

182
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:05,830
It's all my fault.

183
00:11:05,913 --> 00:11:07,557
I wasn't looking where I was going.

184
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:08,500
Sorry again.

185
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,800
Shit. So close.

186
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:15,517
He's left his idiotic friends,
but he's heading back to school.

187
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,012
He's eating lunch there.

188
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,880
So what's my next move?

189
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:22,760
I believe they call him Shigechi.

190
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:27,632
Minutes from now, he'll open that bag
and things will get very complicated.

191
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,230
Damn it.

192
00:11:29,313 --> 00:11:30,143
This is unfathomable.

193
00:11:30,226 --> 00:11:31,056
It's unfathomable.

194
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:47,050
Alrighty,

195
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:51,671
now that I'm in my special hiding spot,
I can finally eat my lunch in peace.

196
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:00,790
Oh, yeah.

197
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:02,432
How did I almost forget?

198
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:05,997
Before I start chowing down on
my food, I need to make coffee.

199
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:09,786
It's not a secret trip to the
gym without a freshly brewed cup.

200
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:17,900
Fortune has smiled on you, Shigechi.

201
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:23,013
Had you peeked inside, my only recourse
would have been to obliterate you.

202
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:31,239
Chosuke, I think this is the place.

203
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:35,140
It's smaller than I thought. What the?

204
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:36,500
Why are they here?

205
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:39,191
I thought these two were blowing them off.

206
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:43,110
Shigechi!

207
00:12:43,193 --> 00:12:44,057
You here or what?

208
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:45,280
Shigechi! Huh?

209
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:47,397
Hey, what are you doing here?

210
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,317
I thought you were going to
get lunch somewhere else.

211
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:50,660
That was the plan.

212
00:12:50,820 --> 00:12:53,677
We couldn't just pass up
free coffee from Cafe Gym.

213
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:56,740
We got 500 yen maku
nochi bentos on the way.

214
00:12:58,380 --> 00:12:59,210
Wow,

215
00:12:59,293 --> 00:13:03,157
I can't believe you two actually showed up
to eat after calling me a stingy bastard.

216
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:05,217
You're a couple of hypocritical pricks.

217
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:07,182
Come on, man, cut us some slack.

218
00:13:07,380 --> 00:13:09,297
Haven't you heard of people
changing their minds?

219
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:11,556
It is a thing that happens, you know.

220
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:14,920
Now what do I do?

221
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:17,297
Offing one of them would
be a walk in the park.

222
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,600
But I can't tackle all three at once.

223
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:22,100
Shit, I was so close, too.

224
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:24,167
She's only centimeters away.

225
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:31,337
Shigechi, you mind grabbing
me a drink on your way back?

226
00:13:31,420 --> 00:13:33,797
And could you make it a
green tea instead of coffee?

227
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:36,440
I'll take a black tea with milk. Really?

228
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,572
Makunochi with milk tea?

229
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:40,053
That sounds disgusting.

230
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:44,057
Shit, he's going to try to eat his
meal right on top of this thing.

231
00:13:44,140 --> 00:13:48,846
If I don't do something fast, he's going
to open the bag right in front of them.

232
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:59,700
Aw, not soy sauce again.

233
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:03,480
They're always giving me
soy sauce with katsu. Huh?

234
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:05,377
That's how you're supposed to eat it.

235
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:07,200
No way. Don't be stupid.

236
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:09,397
Everyone knows it's tonkatsu sauce.

237
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:12,715
Putting soy sauce on tonkatsu
violates all that sacred.

238
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,781
Like it matters.

239
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:21,020
Yes.

240
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,380
Damn it.

241
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:36,160
What the hell?

242
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:49,260
Oh, damn it.

243
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:51,140
What the hell?

244
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:01,940
Just a minute!

245
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:05,220
What exactly do you
think you're doing? Talk!

246
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:06,777
Because from where I'm standing,

247
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:09,437
it looks like you're trying to
steal my sandwich out from under me!

248
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:10,350
As if.

249
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:11,911
Stop being such an idiot.

250
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:14,677
I came over here because I
